{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013FtWKYGHwJ84Mbbejhi57V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that regenerates Unix utilities in Go from C-source-derived specs, verifying parity via differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go implementations, `pkg/` holds shared libraries (sys, format, testutils), `magefiles/` drives orchestration, `docs/` holds specs.\n\n**Implementation status:** Releases 00.0 through 05.0 are marked implemented (specs + code at v1 tags). Release 05.1 (expand, unexpand) is spec_complete with no code yet. Releases 05.2–05.4 and beyond are spec_complete but later priority.\n\n**Current release:** rel05.1 — tab conversion pair (expand, unexpand). Both use cases are spec_complete, code not started.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nrel05.1 is the earliest incomplete release. It has two use cases:\n1. `rel05.1-uc001-expand` — convert tabs to spaces\n2. `rel05.1-uc002-unexpand` — convert spaces to tabs\n\nPer P5 (dependency ordering) and P8 (deterministic ordering), expand comes first alphabetically. Per P2, implementation and tests are separate tasks. With the 1-task limit, I propose the expand implementation task.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/expand (rel05.1-uc001-expand)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find the PRD for expand -- likely prd0XX-expand.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.1-uc001-expand.yaml (use case for expand)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.1.yaml (test suite for rel05.1)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section -- differential testing pattern, SIGPIPE handling)\n      - cmd/fold/main.go (reference implementation of a similar text-stream utility for code style)\n      - cmd/nl/main.go (reference implementation of a similar text-stream utility for code style)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests signature)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/expand/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: expand utility implementation -- tabs to spaces conversion\n      - path: cmd/expand/expand_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gexpand reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement the expand command that converts tabs to spaces, reading from stdin or named files. Default tab stop is 8. Write output to stdout.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Support the -t / --tabs flag accepting either a single number (uniform tab width) or a comma-separated list of tab stop positions. When a list is given, tabs beyond the last stop use the interval between the last two stops.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Support the -i / --initial flag that converts only leading tabs (tabs before the first non-blank character on each line).\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Support --help and --version flags per GNU coreutils conventions. Exit 0 on success, 1 on error.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per the shared SIGPIPE protocol in ARCHITECTURE.yaml.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the same code structure as cmd/fold or cmd/nl -- flag parsing with the flag package, process each input source sequentially, write to os.Stdout.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use the differential testing pattern from ARCHITECTURE.yaml shared_protocols: build the Go binary with testutils.BuildBinary, look up gexpand via exec.LookPath, skip if not found, run testutils.RunDiffTests.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Read all PRD requirements for expand before implementing. The PRD is the source of truth for flag behavior, edge cases, and exit codes. Do not implement behavior not specified in the PRD.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/expand/main.go compiles without errors (go build ./cmd/expand/)\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"expand converts tabs to spaces with default tab stop of 8\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"expand -t N sets uniform tab width; expand -t N1,N2,... sets explicit tab stop positions\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"expand -i converts only leading tabs on each line\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Differential tests in cmd/expand/expand_test.go pass against gexpand (go test ./cmd/expand/)\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Tests skip gracefully with t.Skip when gexpand is not in PATH\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/expand/ reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27534,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27534},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ae3c1b3-b046-4e44-b625-45aa4d7f47aa","uuid":"eb1eb329-156d-4463-beb0-770d235eb76a"}
